  "foaf:name": "Blue Ocean Credits Program",
  "sdo:name": "Blue Ocean Credits Program",
  "sdo:description": "The Blue Ocean Credits Program (BOCP), advances sustainable ocean development by identifying critical marine knowledge, building global capacity, promoting its practical application and pairing cutting-edge reef and blue-carbon science with real financing. BOCP focuses on three pillars: (1) Identifying key ocean knowledge by studying blue carbon ecosystems (mangroves, seagrass, seaweed), monitoring coral biodiversity via initiatives like CRUWITS, and promoting sustainable low-trophic aquaculture for food security and habitat restoration; (2) Building capacity through global workshops, collaborative research with academic and NGO partners, community-based ecosystem management, and youth engagement to cultivate future ocean leaders; and (3) Enhancing knowledge use by developing blue carbon and biodiversity credit systems, deploying AI, remote sensing, and 3D printing for restoration, supporting eco-tourism on restored reefs, and disseminating insights via digital platforms.",
  "sdo:location": "Mexico",
  "sdo:identifier": "80.9",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/blue-ocean-credits-program/",
